<title>AUSTRALIA: AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - June 23.</title>
<headline>AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - June 23.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for June 23</p>
<p>In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	     AH	   PH 13 PCT    PH 14  PCT</p>
<p>    Jun    178.50 -2.5  187.00 -2.5  191.50 -2.5  204.00 -1</p>
<p>    Jul    175.50 -2.5  184.00 -2.5  188.50 -2.5  203.00 -1</p>
<p>    Aug    171.00 -2.5  180.50 -2.5  185.00 -2.5  201.00 -1</p>
<p>    Sept   172.00 -2.5  181.50 -2.5  185.00 -2.5  201.00 -1</p>
<p>    Oct    175.00 -1.5  183.50 -1.5  187.00 -2.5  202.00 -1</p>
<p>    Nov    176.00 -1.5  184.50 -1.5  190.50 -2.5  203.00 -1</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat fell A$1.00 per tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>    National FOB	171.00</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:  Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  146.50	    Port Adelaide	 148.00</p>
<p>    Gladstone     146.75	    Port Giles	    148.75</p>
<p>    Brisbane	144.50	    Wallaroo		146.50</p>
<p> New South Wales			Port Pirie	    143.50</p>
<p>    Newcastle     146.50	    Port Lincoln	  149.75</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   147.00	    Thevenard	     144.75</p>
<p> Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 146.00	     Esperance	    151.25</p>
<p>    Portland	147.00	     Albany		 152.25</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    154.25</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    152.25</p>
<p>AWB MARKET COMMENTARY: Prices were pressured as the US winter wheat harvest continues to move along.  In addition the U.S. and Canadian spring wheat areas were expected to receive timely rain over the weekend.</p>
<p>AWB cash bids for New South Wales A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>			 1996/97 crop		1997/98 crop</p>
<p>    ASW/APW	  A$174.00 Newcastle	A$161.00 Newcastle</p>
<p>    AH1:	     A$184.00 Newcastle	A$174.00 Newcastle</p>
<p>    PH 13:	   A$209.00 Newcastle	A$189.00 Newcastle</p>
<p>    Feed Barley    A$145.00 *State avge    A$125.00 *State avge</p>
<p>			 ex farm June/July	ex farm Nov/Dec</p>
<p>    Sorghum	  A$156.00 Newcastle	No bid</p>
<p>    Triticale	A$158.00 *State avge     A$115.00 *ex farm</p>
<p>			 ex farm June/July	 Dec/Jan</p>
<p>NOTES: The multigrade indicator price represents the AWB's view of the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract fob price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered by the AWB.</p>
<p>ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; PW = Premium White; Percentages =  </p>
<p>protein content.</p>
<p>* Prices vary between regions.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
